---
import LegalPage from "../components/legal/LegalPage.astro";
import { branches, headquarters } from "../data/offices";

const countries = [...new Set(branches.map((office) => office.country))];
const sections = [
  { id: "who-we-are", title: "Who we are" },
  { id: "what-we-collect", title: "What we collect" },
  { id: "how-we-use", title: "How we use it" },
  { id: "sharing", title: "Who we share it with" },
  { id: "transfers", title: "Where it is stored" },
  { id: "retention", title: "How long we keep it" },
  { id: "security", title: "How we protect it" },
  { id: "your-rights", title: "Your choices and rights" },
  { id: "cookies", title: "Cookies" },
  { id: "changes", title: "Changes to this policy" },
  { id: "contact", title: "Contact us" },
];
---
<LegalPage
  title="Privacy Policy — Algorims"
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Algorims collects, uses and protects the personal data you share through algorims.com, and how to reach us about it."
  intro="This policy explains what personal data we collect through algorims.com, why we collect it, who helps us process it, and the choices you have."
  updated="26 November 2026"
  sections={sections}
>
  <section id="who-we-are" aria-labelledby="who-we-are-title">
    <h2 id="who-we-are-title">Who we are</h2>
    <p><strong>Algorims Pte. Ltd.</strong> ("Algorims", "we", "us") is a technology services company headquartered in Singapore, with teams in {countries.join(" and ")}. We operate this website and are responsible for the personal data collected through it.</p>
    <p>This policy covers algorims.com and the forms, chat and booking tools on it. It does not cover data we process for clients under a services agreement; those terms are set out in the agreement.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="what-we-collect" aria-labelledby="what-we-collect-title">
    <h2 id="what-we-collect-title">What we collect</h2>
    <h3>Information you give us</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Contact and enquiry forms</strong>: your name, work email, company, phone or WhatsApp number, the services you are interested in, and your message.</li>
      <li><strong>Support tickets</strong>: your contact details, a description of the issue, its priority, and any file you choose to attach.</li>
      <li><strong>InvoiceNow and WhatsApp audit requests</strong>: your contact details, company details and the information you provide about your current setup.</li>
      <li><strong>Chat</strong>: the messages you type into our chat assistant, when it is available and you choose to use it.</li>
      <li><strong>Meeting bookings</strong>: the details you enter into our scheduling tool when you book a call.</li>
      <li><strong>Email and WhatsApp</strong>: the contents of messages you send us directly.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Information collected automatically</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Campaign details</strong>: if you arrive from an advertisement or a tracked link, the campaign parameters in that link (for example <code>utm_source</code>) are kept for your visit and sent with any form you submit, so we know how you found us.</li>
      <li><strong>Technical data</strong>: like any website, our hosting and font providers receive your IP address, browser type and the page requested in order to deliver the site.</li>
      <li><strong>Optional cookies</strong>: only if you allow them, analytics and advertising tools may record how you use the site. See the <a href="/cookies">cookie policy</a>.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We do not ask for sensitive information such as health or financial account details through this website. Please do not include it in messages or attachments.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="how-we-use" aria-labelledby="how-we-use-title">
    <h2 id="how-we-use-title">How we use it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>To reply to your enquiry, arrange calls, prepare proposals and provide the support you request.</li>
      <li>To contact you by email, phone or WhatsApp about your enquiry, where you have asked us to.</li>
      <li>To understand which pages and campaigns bring useful enquiries, and to improve the site (only with your consent where cookies are involved).</li>
      <li>To keep the site and our systems secure and to prevent spam and misuse.</li>
      <li>To meet our legal, accounting and regulatory obligations.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We rely on your consent, on steps you ask us to take before entering a contract, or on our legitimate interest in running and improving our business. We do not sell your personal data and we do not make decisions about you based solely on automated processing.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="sharing" aria-labelledby="sharing-title">
    <h2 id="sharing-title">Who we share it with</h2>
    <p>We use trusted service providers who process data on our behalf and only for the purposes above:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Web3Forms</strong>, which delivers website form submissions to our inbox.</li>
      <li><strong>Amazon Web Services</strong>, which hosts this website and runs the service that alerts our team to new enquiries.</li>
      <li><strong>Our email and collaboration provider</strong>, where enquiries and support requests are received and handled.</li>
      <li><strong>Zoho Desk</strong>, our support ticketing system for existing clients.</li>
      <li><strong>Chatling</strong>, which provides our chat assistant when it is available and you choose to use it.</li>
      <li><strong>Our scheduling provider</strong>, if you book a meeting through the site.</li>
      <li><strong>Meta (WhatsApp)</strong>, when you message us on WhatsApp.</li>
      <li><strong>Google and Meta advertising tools</strong>, only if they are in use and you have allowed marketing cookies.</li>
      <li><strong>Google Fonts</strong>, which serves the typeface used on this site and receives your IP address when the page loads.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We may also share information within the Algorims group, with professional advisers, or where the law requires it, and with a buyer or successor if our business is reorganised or sold.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="transfers" aria-labelledby="transfers-title">
    <h2 id="transfers-title">Where it is stored</h2>
    <p>Our website is hosted on Amazon Web Services, and our service providers and teams operate in several countries, including Singapore, India and the United States. Your data may therefore be stored or accessed outside the country where you live. When we transfer it, we take reasonable steps, including contractual protections with our providers, to make sure it receives a comparable standard of protection.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="retention" aria-labelledby="retention-title">
    <h2 id="retention-title">How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>We keep enquiry and support records for as long as we need them to respond to you and manage our relationship. If you do not become a client, we aim to delete or anonymise your enquiry within two years of our last contact. Client records are kept for the length of the engagement and as long afterwards as our legal and accounting obligations require.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="security" aria-labelledby="security-title">
    <h2 id="security-title">How we protect it</h2>
    <p>The site is served only over encrypted HTTPS connections. Access to enquiry and support data is limited to the staff who need it, and our systems run on cloud infrastructure with access controls and logging. No method of transmission or storage is completely secure, so we cannot guarantee absolute security, but we work to protect your data and will act promptly if an incident affects it.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="your-rights" aria-labelledby="your-rights-title">
    <h2 id="your-rights-title">Your choices and rights</h2>
    <p>You can ask us to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>tell you what personal data we hold about you and how it has been used;</li>
      <li>correct data that is inaccurate or incomplete;</li>
      <li>delete your data, where we no longer need to keep it;</li>
      <li>stop contacting you, or withdraw any consent you have given.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>If you are in the European Union or the United Kingdom, you may also object to or restrict certain processing, ask for a copy of your data in a portable format, and complain to your local data protection authority.</p>
    <p>You can manage cookies as described in our <a href="/cookies">cookie policy</a>. To exercise any other right, email us at the address below. We may need to confirm your identity first, and we aim to respond within 30 days.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="cookies" aria-labelledby="cookies-title">
    <h2 id="cookies-title">Cookies</h2>
    <p>We use only the browser storage the site needs unless you allow optional tools. The <a href="/cookies">cookie policy</a> lists everything we use and lets you change your choice.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="changes" aria-labelledby="changes-title">
    <h2 id="changes-title">Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>We may update this policy as our services or the law change. The date at the top shows when it was last revised. If a change significantly affects how we use your data, we will make that clear on this page.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="contact" aria-labelledby="contact-title">
    <h2 id="contact-title">Contact us</h2>
    <p>For privacy questions or requests, contact our data protection team:</p>
    <div class="legal-contact">
      <p><strong>Algorims Pte. Ltd.</strong></p>
      <p>{headquarters.lines.join(", ")}</p>
      <p>Email: <a href="mailto:contactus@algorims.com?subject=Privacy%20request">contactus@algorims.com</a></p>
      <p>Existing clients can also reach us at <a href="mailto:support@algorims.com?subject=Privacy%20request">support@algorims.com</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</LegalPage>
